{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Like a bird, wandering, swallow, in flight</b> — four paired elements. The explanations of the names of the birds and beasts that the earlier ones gave are like dreams without interpretation. He mentioned the צפור and the דרור because they dwell in houses with people and must quickly fly from place to place because of passersby; so a baseless curse quickly comes upon the fool who curses, and does not come upon the one who is cursed. It is written with לא [spelled לא אל\"ף?], to indicate that it comes upon the one who curses and does not come upon the one who is cursed."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The phrase 'וכתיב לא באל״ף' is obscure; it appears to refer to the לא in the verse, but the exact argument is unclear. Rendered hyper-literally. Also, the phrase 'והעד: אל תען כסיל' (\"and the witness: do not answer a fool\") appears to cite Proverbs 26:4 as supporting evidence but its connection to the argument is cryptic; rendered literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:49.230939985Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}